{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 211, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At already-large learning rates (0.0774-1) a further increase destabilizes Adam training and collapses accuracy (e.g. exp 12: -53.7 on segment)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reducing a divergent learning rate recovers training, giving large gains (exps 14-16) unlike reductions elsewhere."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "With tiny learning rates the network is undertrained after 243 epochs, so increasing the rate helps a lot (exps 9-10)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Lowering an already-small learning rate pushes further into undertraining (exps 18-19)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Once the L2 penalty is large, increasing it further causes heavy underfitting (exps 81-86), whereas at small alpha the change is negligible."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "down", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Relaxing an overly strong L2 penalty restores model capacity and yields big gains (exps 93-96)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper ReLU nets are less stable at high learning rates, so adding a layer there is harmful (exps 43-44)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At low learning rates extra depth add